course: dictionary
lesson: 7170
title: Permanent, meaning for ever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Permanent» means lasting for ever, or for a very long time, and not changing. Its opposite is temporary, which means it lasts only a short while.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «The UN Security Council has five permanent members» tells you the members stay in their seats and do not change, so permanent means lasting and not changing.
explain: A permanent marker does not wash off. A permanent change cannot be undone, so the clue is always whether the thing can be reversed. To check your meaning, swap in «for a very long time» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Permanent» means lasting for ever or for a very long time.
fact: «Permanent teeth» are the grown-up teeth that come in behind the baby teeth.
fact: A «permanent change» cannot be undone, like cooking an egg.
fact: «Permanent» is the opposite of «temporary».
fact: A «permanent job» has no planned end date.
exercise: Which marker should you use to write on a box so the writing stays? | A whiteboard pen | *A permanent marker | A washable marker | A pencil
exercise: «The UN Security Council has five permanent members.» What does permanent mean here? | Members who are very loud | Members who wear name badges | *Members who stay and do not change | Members who only come for one meeting
exercise: Which of these is a permanent change? | Blowing up a balloon | Folding a paper plane | Building a sandcastle | *Cooking an egg
test: «At about six, the first grown-up back teeth come in behind the baby teeth, so many people do not realise they are permanent.» Which teeth are called permanent? | Baby teeth | *Grown-up teeth that come in behind the baby teeth | Teeth that fall out when you are six | Teeth that grow only in summer
test: Which word means the opposite of permanent? | Lasting | Strong | Forever | *Temporary
exam: Jayden says a permanent job has a planned end date. Is he right? | Yes, a permanent job always ends in a year | *No, a permanent job has no planned end | No, permanent means made of paper | Yes, every job has an end date
